Track 2: Tshe-Tshe Hiding-Place
- Story & Context: Mbeki hid his shame in the forgotten sub-basements of the vault, crafting makeshift kalimbas from discarded ventilation brackets to drown out his confession of deserting the northern patrol. A security sensor caught the rhythmic metallic tapping of his labor, reporting it as a mechanical error while Mbeki wept into the hollow resonance of a vent. "My hands map the ghosts of the soil where nothing stays still," he crooned, his voice weaving through the sharp, synthetic pulse of a misaligned oscillator.
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: A grainy, high-contrast silhouette of a man hunched over a collection of shimmering metallic scrap-instruments in a dark, vaulted corridor.

Track 3: Does the archive feel the thaw?
- Story & Context: The vault sensors triggered a false alarm as the entire building began to resonate with the frequency of a thousand germinating beans, effectively dissolving the border between the machine and the forest. The archivists found the main server room overflowing with thick, verdant kudzu that pulsed in time with the decaying remnants of a looped Juno melody. "Will you dream of rain when the walls finally crack?" the voice boomed over the intercom, leaving the curators to wonder if the seeds were finally keeping their promise to reclaim the world.
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: A massive, brutalist concrete wall being torn apart by thick, vibrant green vines that seem to be glowing with an internal, soft bioluminescence.

